  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Poverty Action Lab Southeast Asia - Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Poverty Action Lab Southeast Asia (J-PAL SEA) Phase 2 aims to help the Government of Indonesia (GOI) create a more productive, inclusive Indonesia by pursuing the twin objectives of strengthening evidence-informed policymaking and increasing the capacity of Indonesian and regional researchers and policymakers to generate, use and design high-quality economic policy research. Phase 2 will focus on three core activities i.e. research, policy outreach and capacity building. It will build on the strong results achieved during the Phase 1 which contributed to major policy impacts in Indonesia, including helping GOI to scale-up social programs reaching some 65 million Indonesians. Phase 2 will expand the thematic scope of J-PAL SEA&#x2019;s works from the current phase&#x2019;s focus on social programs to policy questions relating to inclusive growth, human capital and employment, domestic resource mobilisation and inclusion.</narrative>
  </description>
